    Better performance than gp2
    Lower cost 💰
    You can configure IOPS & throughput separately

    👉 🔥 Most commonly used

🔹 2) Provisioned IOPS SSD
    ✅ io1
    High performance SSD
    Used for critical applications
    ✅ io2
    Higher durability & performance than io1
    Used for mission-critical databases

    👉 Example:

    Banking systems
    High-end databases
🔹 3) HDD (Hard Disk Drives)
    ✅ st1 (Throughput Optimized HDD)
    Good for large data workloads
    High throughput

    👉 Use cases:

    Big data
    Logs processing
    ✅ sc1 (Cold HDD)
    Lowest cost 💰
    Used for infrequently accessed data
🔹 4) Magnetic (Standard)
    ✅ Standard (Magnetic)
    Old generation
    Low performance
    Rarely used now ❌

